      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "A triangle has area $40\\text{ cm}^2$, sides $a = 10\\text{ cm}$ and $b = 16\\text{ cm}$. What is the included angle $C$?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$30°$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$90°$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$45°$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$60°$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "a",
      "explanation": "$40 = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 16 \\times \\sin C$, so $\\sin C = \\frac{40}{80} = 0.5$, giving $C = 30°$."
    }
  ]
